  "clf_pinned_echo": {
   "text": "\"  \n<<The Cost of Neglecting Study>>  \nNot studying leads to poor performance and wasted time. When you skip lessons or assignments, you miss out on important knowledge that can help you in the long run. It's like building a house without a foundation—your skills and understanding will not be solid. Studying regularly helps you prepare for exams and future challenges. It also builds discipline and responsibility. If you don't study, you may struggle to keep up with your work and feel behind. It's better to invest time in studying now than to face the consequences later.  \n\n******  \n\n<<The Consequences of Not Studying>>  \nNot studying results in lower grades and a lack of understanding. Without proper study, you may not be able to grasp the material and perform well in exams. It also affects your confidence and motivation. Studying helps you develop a habit of learning and staying focused. If you don't study, you may feel frustrated and lose interest in your subjects. It's important to take responsibility for your learning and make time for study. By studying, you are setting yourself up for success in the future.  \n\"",
